They are therefore NOT covered by the AGPL-3.0 grant above. This project cannot
license what it does not own, and nothing here grants anyone permission to copy,
redistribute, or reuse those files. If you fork or redistribute this software,
that permission is yours to obtain or yours to do without.

Every affected file lives in exactly two directories:

    public/audio/     five short interface sounds
    assets/music/     one background track

Deleting both removes all of it. The application detects their absence and runs
silently; no code change is needed.

If you hold the rights to this audio and want it removed, open an issue on the
repository or contact the owner, and it will be taken down.
